## Two-phase write

Every write follows this path. Drawing or building it differently breaks the security model.

1. Agent proposes → signed, expiring proposal token. **Nothing has changed yet.**
2. Named approver role reviews, with the context needed to decide — not just the proposed action.
3. Approval re-binds the template **from scratch** from `{templateId, params}` and **re-checks the role** before executing.
4. Execution is audited: who, what, when, what they saw.

## Approval path load

An approval path that becomes a bottleneck will be routed around, and a gate that is routed around is worse than no gate because it is still on the architecture diagram.

